566
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:44,490
No, not a competition.

567
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:48,989
Ever since I was little, I've loved meat so much.

568
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:53,229
I prefer it really thick, half meat and half broth.

569
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:55,069
Like a super rich, traditional cheonggukjang?

570
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:56,310
Yes, it should be really thick.

571
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,469
- Loaded with meat. - Right.

572
00:19:57,470 --> 00:19:59,299
- Cooked down low. - Exactly.

573
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,800
- Same stew, different style. - Yes.

574
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:02,140
Same stew, different style?

575
00:20:02,810 --> 00:20:04,010
Same stew, different...

576
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:06,509
- Same stew, different style. - Same stew, different style.

577
00:20:06,510 --> 00:20:08,549
- Okay. - Same stew, different style. Yes.

578
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:09,979
Sanghyeon, I hear your mom excels at other dishes...

579
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:12,150
- besides cheonggukjang. - Yes.

580
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:16,420
That's right. Braised back ribs, and the beef short ribs my dad makes.

581
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:19,420
- Gosh. - This was made at home?

582
00:20:19,490 --> 00:20:22,130
Yes. My dad is really interested in cooking,

583
00:20:22,730 --> 00:20:24,359
and he even plans to get...

584
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:25,999
- culinary certifications later on. - Really?

585
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,730
- Gosh. - We have a sous-vide machine.

586
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,030
- Really? - Yes.

587
00:20:29,130 --> 00:20:31,069
- A sous-vide machine at home? - Yes.

588
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:32,070
He's serious about it.

589
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:37,640
When he said he wanted to buy that, did your mom agree easily?

590
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:39,880
Going, "How much is it?"

591
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:44,310
My mom bakes a lot,

592
00:20:44,450 --> 00:20:46,149
- so we have a big oven at home too. - Baking.

593
00:20:46,150 --> 00:20:50,650
The kitchen is completely packed with all kinds of cooking equipment.

594
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:52,766
Then you must miss home-cooked meals even more.

595
00:20:52,790 --> 00:20:54,219
You must have eaten so well at home.

596
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,259
That's awesome.

597
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:59,300
My dad grilled lamb chops and things like that.

598
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:01,830
- Right. - Like grilled lamb ribs.

599
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:05,369
Dads in American movies are always doing that.

600
00:21:05,370 --> 00:21:06,370
Yes, exactly like that.

601
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,599
Right, my dad does that too.

602
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:08,669
Just like in movies,

603
00:21:08,670 --> 00:21:10,209
- on the patio in the yard. - In the yard.

604
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:13,540
A lot of houses overseas are like that.

605
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:16,649
Chenle, your mom's a great cook too, isn't she?

606
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:17,650
- Of course she is. - Actually,

607
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:21,619
Chenle brought a photo of his home cooking.

608
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:23,450
Let's take a look and talk about it.

609
00:21:24,090 --> 00:21:27,390
- Gosh. - Wait, what is this?

610
00:21:27,690 --> 00:21:29,689
You don't eat like this every day, right? Only on special occasions?

611
00:21:29,690 --> 00:21:31,060
No, no, no. On regular days.

612
00:21:31,530 --> 00:21:32,530
Regular days?

613
00:21:32,531 --> 00:21:34,899
Fish in season sometimes. For example,

614
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:36,299
- Even in season? - sometimes...

615
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:38,139
Typically, we eat a lot of crucian carp...

616
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:40,299
- or pomfret. - Oh, steamed crucian carp?

617
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:41,369
- Pomfret is quite expensive. - And...

618
00:21:41,370 --> 00:21:43,570
- And hairtail, too. - we eat hairtail too.

619
00:21:44,010 --> 00:21:46,179
My mom goes grocery shopping every morning.

620
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:47,839
(A mom-made meal full of care, nutrition, and love)

621
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:50,049
I think I ate steak often.

622
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:52,019
- Right, steak. - Steak?

623
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:55,419
My dad always bought giant steaks this big.

624
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:58,360
So we ate that a lot. And we always had that with...

625
00:21:58,690 --> 00:22:00,519
- asparagus. - Asparagus.

626
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:02,589
- Asparagus. - Yes.

627
00:22:02,590 --> 00:22:05,229
- Asparagus. - Asparagus.

628
00:22:05,230 --> 00:22:06,399
We ate it with asparagus.

629
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:08,670
- Asparagus. - Asparagus.

630
00:22:08,770 --> 00:22:11,739
When I want home cooking, I go to my grandmother's.

631
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:13,580
What style of food does your grandmother make?

632
00:22:14,070 --> 00:22:15,809
I really love eel.

633
00:22:15,810 --> 00:22:17,309
Oh, eel. I love eel too.

634
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:22,050
I love eel so much, so she always has it ready when I go over.

635
00:22:22,150 --> 00:22:25,580
I never have to ask. And the soup is always different.

636
00:22:26,050 --> 00:22:27,579
- Whatever soup comes out. - Yes.

637
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:28,660
- Soup of the day. - Right.

638
00:22:28,850 --> 00:22:29,850
You never know.

639
00:22:30,150 --> 00:22:31,789
- Gosh. - Grandmother!

640
00:22:31,790 --> 00:22:33,019
I see acorn jelly.

641
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:34,220
- Crab, crab. - Crab?

642
00:22:34,490 --> 00:22:36,559
- Spicy blue crab stew? - LA-style grilled beef short rib.

643
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,659
The soup changed again.

644
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:40,559
Right, exactly. You never know what kind of soup it is.

645
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:41,799
The eel is literally...

646
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:43,230
- just grilled eel. - Yes.

647
00:22:43,330 --> 00:22:45,540
- Gosh. - What are those, chestnuts?

648
00:22:45,940 --> 00:22:49,540
- Acorn jelly? - Acorn jelly. She gathers acorns...

649
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:51,830
- She makes it from scratch? - She makes it all.

650
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:54,360
- She makes it all herself. - That really takes time.

651
00:22:54,950 --> 00:22:57,850
- Gosh, that's amazing. - That was wonderful to see.

652
00:22:58,050 --> 00:23:01,650
I'm curious about Chanelle too. What's your family's signature dish?

653
00:23:01,690 --> 00:23:05,460
We have a big family. My grandmother had ten kids.

654
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:08,230
- Really? That's a huge family. - Ten?

655
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:09,829
Which child was your dad?

656
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:10,830
- The 2nd. - The 2nd?

657
00:23:10,831 --> 00:23:12,530
So I have over 20 cousins.

658
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:13,860
They're all different ages.

659
00:23:13,861 --> 00:23:15,530
It feels like having lots of friends.

660
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:21,509
So my grandma cooked a lot, and there was one unusual dish.

661
00:23:21,510 --> 00:23:22,510
What kind of dish?

662
00:23:22,810 --> 00:23:24,610
- Frog eye salad. - Frog eye?

663
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:26,310
- Another eye? An eye again? - What?

664
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:27,680
- Frog eyes? - Frog eyes?

665
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:29,909
- A real frog? - Frog eyes?

666
00:23:29,910 --> 00:23:31,550
(It is frog eye salad.)

667
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:33,149
Wait, isn't that rice?

668
00:23:33,150 --> 00:23:34,950
- Macaroni? - It kind of looks like broccoli.

669
00:23:35,390 --> 00:23:36,826
- At least it's not real frog eyes. - It's...

670
00:23:36,850 --> 00:23:41,020
No, it got that name because it's tiny, about this size.

671
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:46,330
You put pudding in custard, and if you wait, it expands.

672
00:23:46,830 --> 00:23:47,899
- Once it expands, - Oh, it expands.

673
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:50,930
- it looks a bit like frog eyeballs. - Like frog eyeballs?

674
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:56,409
It has fruit, vanilla pudding, and even marshmallows.

675
00:23:56,410 --> 00:23:57,809
- Marshmallows? - Then, it's dessert.

676
00:23:57,810 --> 00:23:59,679
- It's a dessert, totally a dessert. - Fascinating.

677
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,550
What's the texture like?

678
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,679
- It's chewy at first, - Chewy?

679
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:05,879
- and as there are marshmallows, - Because it's made from pasta...

680
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:06,880
you can melt it.

681
00:24:08,290 --> 00:24:09,290
I'm curious.

682
00:24:09,590 --> 00:24:10,690
I'm so curious.

683
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:14,019
- For me, sambal? I love spicy food. - Sambal?

684
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:16,690
Sambal matah? It's different from others.

685
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:18,329
It's not stir-fried or deep-fried.

686
00:24:18,330 --> 00:24:19,376
- You should add raw chili peppers. - You...

687
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:20,400
You grind them up right away?

688
00:24:20,401 --> 00:24:21,700
Right, raw chili peppers.

689
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:27,170
I recently went to Bali, and they kept feeding me. I couldn't say no.

690
00:24:27,570 --> 00:24:28,709
- You have to eat a lot... - You're right.

691
00:24:28,710 --> 00:24:29,710
When you can.

692
00:24:29,910 --> 00:24:31,110
Oh, she's right.

693
00:24:31,140 --> 00:24:32,540
How many bowls of rice did you eat?

694
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:35,480
It wasn't even measured in rice bowls. It was like...

695
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:36,780
- Right. - A big bowl?

696
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:38,520
Like a big stainless-steel bowl.

697
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:41,020
It's a bowl. It's the bowl.

698
00:24:41,050 --> 00:24:42,850
- Are you going to grow even taller? - Right.

699
00:24:43,390 --> 00:24:46,620
Talking about home-cooked meals makes me think of my parents.

700
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:48,329
Suddenly, I miss my mom.

701
00:24:48,330 --> 00:24:51,699
It's been so long since you've eaten home cooking while promoting.

702
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:52,729
You guys have to buy food outside.

703
00:24:52,730 --> 00:24:56,929
Hometowns are far and delivery is the norm,

704
00:24:56,930 --> 00:24:59,400
so what does home food mean to you?

705
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:01,839
- I'd say it's happiness. - Happiness?

706
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:04,639
Because that happiness means having fun while having...

707
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:09,350
a warm meal and chatting together.

708
00:25:09,380 --> 00:25:13,120
I think this whole time itself is real happiness.

709
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:19,559
It gives you a sense of security that lets you stay a kid,

710
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:20,959
- and I think... - A sense of security.

711
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:22,430
There's also a certain warmth to it.

712
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:26,399
Right, you always have to act like a grown-up,

713
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:27,400
but when you go home, you can...

714
00:25:27,401 --> 00:25:30,300
- just be completely relaxed. - You're right.

715
00:25:30,870 --> 00:25:32,670
To me, home-cooked food is love.

716
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,399
- It's love. - It's love, pure love.

717
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:39,509
When I eat a home-cooked meal, I feel loved by my family.

718
00:25:39,510 --> 00:25:42,780
Right. Even if you misbehaved, they still make it for you.

719
00:25:42,810 --> 00:25:44,009
- They do. Mom always makes it. - Right.

720
00:25:44,010 --> 00:25:45,120
Why? Because it's love.

721
00:25:45,350 --> 00:25:46,550
Mom, Dad, I love you.

722
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:48,320
So cute.

723
00:25:48,590 --> 00:25:52,019
Good job, good job.

724
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:54,819
I think home-cooked food is a restart to me.

725
00:25:54,820 --> 00:25:55,989
A kind of restart?

726
00:25:55,990 --> 00:25:59,399
We're busy and we get exhausted a lot,

727
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,999
but eating a home-cooked meal gives me that boost.

728
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:03,000
That boost.

729
00:26:03,230 --> 00:26:04,230
It gives you energy.

730
00:26:04,231 --> 00:26:05,440
And you can recharge.

731
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:08,509
Home-cooked food is a safe place. A safe place.

732
00:26:08,510 --> 00:26:09,510
- Safety. - For me...

733
00:26:09,511 --> 00:26:10,970
- Safety. - Yes, safety.

734
00:26:11,010 --> 00:26:13,679
- Since you're with people you love, - Right.

735
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:15,509
It makes you feel safe.

736
00:26:15,510 --> 00:26:18,050
- Yes. - Home-cooked food is romance.

737
00:26:18,580 --> 00:26:19,580
Romance.

738
00:26:20,650 --> 00:26:22,289
To me, I think home-cooked food...

739
00:26:22,290 --> 00:26:24,550
- is devotion. - Devotion.

740
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:28,329
Talking about home-cooked food makes me miss my parents.

741
00:26:28,330 --> 00:26:31,290
- Truly. - Mom, Mom.

742
00:26:32,060 --> 00:26:33,330
Mom and Dad.

743
00:26:33,430 --> 00:26:35,169
(Lele is feeling emotional.)

744
00:26:35,170 --> 00:26:36,170
What?

745
00:26:37,370 --> 00:26:39,370
I feel so shy all of a sudden.

746
00:26:39,470 --> 00:26:40,540
- Were you shy? - Yes.

747
00:26:40,700 --> 00:26:42,270
Should I do it for you? Thank you.

748
00:26:42,870 --> 00:26:43,870
Thank you.

749
00:26:45,540 --> 00:26:46,940
(Laughing)

750
00:26:47,980 --> 00:26:49,449
- Thank you for letting us... - Mom and Dad.

751
00:26:49,450 --> 00:26:50,680
Meet Carmen here.

752
00:26:51,150 --> 00:26:56,149
Carmen is doing well here. Thank you. I love you.

753
00:26:56,150 --> 00:26:58,519
(Thank you and I love you.)

754
00:26:58,520 --> 00:26:59,690
I love you.

755
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,160
Mom and Dad.

756
00:27:01,161 --> 00:27:04,859
I'm eating well. I'm good and staying strong.

757
00:27:04,860 --> 00:27:06,800
So don't worry. Love you.

758
00:27:08,930 --> 00:27:12,699
Mom, Dad, I'm eating really well, so don't worry,

759
00:27:12,700 --> 00:27:14,639
and let's see each other and eat together soon.

760
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:15,640
I love you so much.

761
00:27:15,641 --> 00:27:18,240
(I love you so much.)

762
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:22,550
Thank you for serving delicious food for a long time for me.

763
00:27:23,150 --> 00:27:25,320
(Our Lele is such a grown-up.)

764
00:27:25,520 --> 00:27:29,289
Mom, I'm eating well, and I know you worry a lot.

765
00:27:29,290 --> 00:27:32,020
Still, I'm eating more than at home, so don't worry.

766
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:36,730
I'm becoming a better person, so don't worry,

767
