Are you all listening, everyone? It's so lovely. I love this song.

1526
00:55:48,550 --> 00:55:49,550
It's so good.

1527
00:55:49,620 --> 00:55:51,189
- It really gets stuck in your head. - It's so catchy.

1528
00:55:51,190 --> 00:55:52,190
Thank you.

1529
00:55:52,191 --> 00:55:56,159
Sharing these warm stories made it feel so cozy in here,

1530
00:55:56,160 --> 00:55:58,590
even though it's gotten chilly outside.

1531
00:55:58,730 --> 00:56:01,299
For today's sign-off, let's say something like, "I'm home."

1532
00:56:01,300 --> 00:56:02,629
- Sounds good. - Okay.

1533
00:56:02,630 --> 00:56:03,930
- I'm home. - Okay.

1534
00:56:05,400 --> 00:56:07,470
- I'm home. - I'm home.

1535
00:56:07,800 --> 00:56:10,146
- I love you, Mom. I love you, Dad. - Poong, give me an allowance.

1536
00:56:10,170 --> 00:56:11,610
Mom, make me food.

1537
00:56:11,840 --> 00:56:14,340
Poong, give me an allowance. Poong.

1538
00:56:14,810 --> 00:56:16,540
- Poong, some allowance. - Am I your dad?

1539
00:56:18,080 --> 00:56:21,280
(An incident that shook the peaceful table)

1540
00:56:24,390 --> 00:56:25,390
Today's theme is...

1541
00:56:25,620 --> 00:56:29,159
Believe it or not, the Strange Table.

1542
00:56:29,160 --> 00:56:30,429
(Trembling)

1543
00:56:30,430 --> 00:56:32,490
- I think Carmen will like this. - That's right.

1544
00:56:33,030 --> 00:56:34,760
New family members, please come in.

1545
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:36,430
- Come on in. - Welcome.

1546
00:56:36,700 --> 00:56:38,270
Oh, that's scary, scary, scary.

1547
00:56:38,330 --> 00:56:39,730
- Chucky, Chucky. - Chucky, Chucky.

1548
00:56:40,030 --> 00:56:41,870
I don't really believe in ghosts either.

1549
00:56:42,070 --> 00:56:43,240
Wait, what is that?

1550
00:56:44,970 --> 00:56:47,180
(Scared to death)

1551
00:56:47,340 --> 00:56:48,409
You said you don't believe in them.

1552
00:56:48,410 --> 00:56:49,740
It's scary.

1553
00:56:49,780 --> 00:56:52,450
There are lots of superstitions about food.

1554
00:56:52,510 --> 00:56:54,750
If you eat bread before a test, you get a zero.

1555
00:56:55,050 --> 00:56:58,350
We have big family Thanksgivings. Turkey is a must.

1556
00:56:58,490 --> 00:56:59,490
Who gets the legs?

1557
00:56:59,990 --> 00:57:02,260
- The legs? Well... - Is it a war? A war?

1558
00:57:02,520 --> 00:57:05,390
- Who will make the Special Recipe? - Gosh.

1559
00:57:05,430 --> 00:57:06,960
- Gosh, it's you! - It's me.

1560
00:57:07,360 --> 00:57:08,500
What is your lucky dish?

1561
00:57:08,760 --> 00:57:10,000
- Cheese, strawberries. - Okay.

1562
00:57:10,270 --> 00:57:12,330
Is it seasoned four-leaf clovers or something?

1563
00:57:12,470 --> 00:57:15,700
It works, it doesn't, it works, it doesn't.

1564
00:57:16,140 --> 00:57:17,709
Have a great day today.

1565
00:57:17,710 --> 00:57:20,280
(What's the lucky recipe starting in earnest?)

1566
00:57:21,410 --> 00:57:24,279
Gosh. This is practically an Italian restaurant.

1567
00:57:24,280 --> 00:57:25,280
(Tasting)

1568
00:57:26,110 --> 00:57:29,050
- Who made this? - I ate everything up.

1569
00:57:29,220 --> 00:57:31,920
- I'm torn on changing first place. - Is it that good?

1570
00:57:32,290 --> 00:57:33,290
This is first place.

1571
00:57:33,291 --> 00:57:34,319
- First place? - First place.

1572
00:57:34,320 --> 00:57:35,689
(What is the strangest lucky food of all time?)

1573
00:57:35,690 --> 00:57:37,690
- It's so good. - Eat it all for good luck.
